---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
// What src/scripts/count.js sends. tests/privacy-hosts.test.mjs fails if the
// site's code starts talking to an outside host this page doesn't name.
const updated = '2026-11-06';
---
<Base title="Privacy" description="What marsh.city counts, what it doesn't, and who does the counting.">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p class="tagline">What this site counts and what it leaves alone.</p>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>What's counted</h2>
    <p>
      Each time a page on marsh.city loads, it sends one anonymous count to
      <a href="https://www.goatcounter.com/">GoatCounter</a>, a small open-source analytics
      service, at marshcity.goatcounter.com. The count carries two things:
    </p>
    {/* Plain text, no <code>: VoiceOver splits a sentence into separate swipes at each inline code element (a11y/privacy.txt). */}
    <ul>
      <li>the page's address, without any search terms or section link added to the end</li>
      <li>the name of the site that linked you here, such as www.linkedin.com, without the page you came from</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Like any web server, GoatCounter sees the request your browser makes. From it,
      GoatCounter works out your country and your browser and operating system name and
      version, and keeps only those, grouped by the hour. To tell one visit from several, it holds a temporary
      code in memory for eight hours and never writes it to disk.
      Its <a href="https://www.goatcounter.com/privacy">privacy policy</a> has the details.
    </p>

    <h2>What isn't</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No cookies, and nothing is stored in your browser for counting.</li>
      <li>No ID that follows you from visit to visit or site to site.</li>
      <li>Your IP address isn't stored, by me or by GoatCounter.</li>
      <li>Nothing you do inside the apps on this site (the radio, games and tools) is counted.</li>
      <li>If your browser sends Global Privacy Control or Do Not Track, nothing is counted at all.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Other services pages use</h2>
    <p>
      Pages with diagrams load the Mermaid drawing library from jsDelivr at cdn.jsdelivr.net,
      which sees the request the way any web server does.
      Fonts and everything else come from marsh.city itself, which is hosted on GitHub Pages;
      like any web host, GitHub sees each request your browser makes.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>Email <a href="mailto:jason@marsh.city">jason@marsh.city</a>.</p>
  </div>

  <p style="color: var(--fg-soft); font-size: 0.85rem; font-family: var(--font-mono); margin-top: 3rem;">
    Updated {updated}
  </p>
</Base>
